'''Sonic Cat''' is a [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cat]] that can be obtained when beating any stage in [[Sonic the Hedgehog Collaboration Event#Green Hill Zone|Green Hill Zone]] during the [[Sonic the Hedgehog Collaboration Event]]. It was added in [[Version 14.4 Update|Version 14.4]] for [[Nyanko Daisensou|BJCP]] and [[Version 14.5 Update|Version 14.5]] for [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 807
|rarity = RR
|name1 = Sonic Cat
|name2 = Sonic Cat CC
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Sonic Cat CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Unlike the other non-Uber units in the Sonic Collaboration Event, Sonic Cat has different stats between forms, with different abilities as well.

==='''Normal Form'''===
Sonic Cat is meant to function as an anti-[[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] melee attacker. However, it has an abysmal range value of 130, a somewhat long cooldown and Single Attack, meaning anything beyond [[Cyberhorn]] or short-ranged Alien peons like Star Peng will prove to be risky matchups. Players will usually resort to [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]] instead, as it has more powerful Area Attacks at longer range. It is also outclassed by [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]], whose True Form isn't difficult to obtain and is an all-round superior alternative with its wide assortment of abilities.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Sonic Cat CC functions as an anti-Alien meatshield. Despite its misleading animations, Sonic Cat CC has an abysmally slow speed of 8. This unit is, for all intents and purposes, completely useless and outclassed by [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]]. While Sonic Cat CC has the advantage in HP and the [[Resistant]] ability, Catellite is cheaper, moves faster and has a shorter cooldown time. Its Strong ability loses out on defense, but can contribute significantly more damage, has a variety of immunities (Slow/Weaken). + levels and Talents further widening their performance gap. [[Jetpack Cat (Rare Cat)|Jetpack Cat]] further outclasses it in its own no-gacha niche during late-game.

